{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1500859-can-the-mage-spheres-affect-imbued","id":1500859,"title":"Can the Mage Spheres affect Imbued?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-01-20T12:32:47-08:00","id":1500859,"title":"Can the Mage Spheres affect Imbued?","content":"Friend of mine was waning to do some experimentation with different game lines, but we've been having some trouble with the Imbued from Hunter. He had the idea to try and basically shapeshift an Imbued into a monster for a story, as well as a small scene of another Imbued using magic.<br /> <br /> However, we can't really figure if the rules would allow this or not; according to the Hunter books, the Imbued are <i>supposed</i> to be immune to anything supernatural that can change their body or soul. At the same time though, the Hunter books do contradict the other game lines in some ways, such as using level 5 edges to turn a mage back into a normal human. We also couldn't quite find anything saying that the Imbued couldn't use magic, though to be fair we most likely have missed something.<br /> <br /> So what's the verdict? Would it be possible for a Mage to transform an Imbued into a monster in some way, or no? What about an Imbued using magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27528-just-some-guy","name":"Just Some Guy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T13:05:49-08:00","id":1500860,"title":"","content":"I'd use similar guidelines to Imbued being reshaped via Vicissitude - roll Conviction w/o spending any, and any successes cancel out the attempt on a one for one basis. Their fellow hunters can also heal them of the effect in question. The only way that these hunters get turned into monsters is if they choose to become as such, and even then, it's only by accepting demonic influence for Rank 5 Edges (there's a book about it - Fall From Grace). What would also be interesting/muddying the waters is if this physical change convinced the poor, ignorant soul that they're beyond help, and they accept said demon out of hopelessness. Then you have to deal with their getting, essentially, an Apocalyptic form a la D:tF, as well as potentially being host to a being on the level of one of the Earthbound.<br /> <br /> tl;dr yes but they probably won't be staying that way and it could be a source of angst for them, especially martyrs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T13:07:33-08:00","id":1500861,"title":"","content":"The Imbued have limited protections against supernatural powers. The most ironclad protection they have is that if they spend a point of Conviction, you don't get to control their mind for the duration. Related to that, if they spend a Conviction to activate their Sight, your illusions won't receive them. But in both cases, if they <i>don't</i> spend the Conviction, they don't get the immunity. <br /> <br /> I could see a houserule that provides the Imbued with countermagick equal to their highest Virtue if they spend a point of Conviction to activate it, and if the Effect in question is directly targeting the Imbued in question. This would be in addition to the above immunities, and would serve as a general \u201cthey're anti-mages\u201d rule. <br /> <br /> The other immunity that the Imbued have is that they can't <i>become</i> supernatural entities: attempts to Embrace them will always lead to a corpse, not a new Kindred; thru never Awaken, go through a Chrysalis, or experience a First Change. According to comments made by the developers on the original White Wolf forums, they can't use any Numina either; not even True Faith. (I'm pretty sure that the ensuing discussion informed the section in the Player's Guide about the Imbued and Faith.) It was part of a mindset at the time that if you allowed any sort of access to supernatural powers other than the Edges, then players would run hog-wild with it and <i>every</i> Imbued would be slinging spells. So at first glance, the answer would seem to be that no, the Imbued don't get access to magic \u2014 not even <i>static</i> magic. <br /> <br /> But I'm not one to slam the door on an idea if I can avoid it. So I'll note that one of the ways to unlock the fifth dot of your Edges is to get a demon to do it for you. (Here, \u201cdemon\u201d refers to a malevolent supernatural entity that's at odds with the forces responsible for the Imbuement.) Extending that idea, I would allow an Imbued who has lost his way so be able to bargain with demonic forces for power: Infernal Investments, if you will. The result would likely be incompatible with the Imbuement: at a minimum, spending any Inspiration for any purpose whatsoever would also disable any Infernal Investments the Imbued may have received; or you might have to spend a point of Inspiration to disable any supernatural powers you've acquired before you can spend Inspiration on anything else. So yeah; if you're willing to put up with a few extra headaches, I could see an Imbued using magic; just not Awakened Magick. <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-20T15:19:39-08:00","id":1500871,"title":"","content":"Activating Second Sight doesn't just protect the Imbued from mind control powers, it also protects them from having their bodies controlled (questionable if shape shifting should apply there), and a few other things. But the &quot;it needs to be active&quot; is still the important point here. If an Imbued doesn't manage to get it up (or doesn't activate an Edge that could protect them) then they have no special defenses against Sphere magic.<br /> <br /> Another important point, is that those protections are retroactive. Anything effects that the Imbued are immune to while Second Sight is active will also end immediately if they weren't protected and they activate it at a later time (there's a story about a Toreador that found this out in a bad way when using Presence to get their own personal magical bodyguard doesn't end well when their Presence and blood bonding all snapped).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T10:50:05-08:00","id":1501723,"title":"","content":"The Imbued (from the Reckoning books, guides and supplements) do seem - from the stories in the books, from their capabilities and abilities, and from related themes - like they could have some tangible resistance to special and supernatural powers or abilities, or to magic and spells, in some situations or under some circumstances. But it is not that noteworthy when compared to overall capabilities and skills of Mages (whether Tradition Mages, Nephandi Mages, or Technocrats).<br /> <br /> In fact, overall the Imbued could be considered to have a distinctly lower power level and a smaller variety of abilities and methods compared to Tradition Mages, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-30-2023, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-30T15:40:52-08:00","id":1501752,"title":"","content":"The Imbued are absolutely weaker than the main PC supernaturals of the WoD. They have good powers for punching above their power level against supernaturals, but they're so focused on that, that they have very little that helps them do anything else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T02:51:43-08:00","id":1501792,"title":"","content":"Joining with the others above, that yes the mage could affect them, but when Conviction is spent the power would be broken.<br /> <br /> Also the no to doing magic - however in some of the fiction and views of the Awakened, they do mistake the Imbued for those doing magic. One main part of the HtR narrative is that the supernatural do not know or understand what the Imbued are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26145-babi_gog","name":"babi_gog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-01-31T08:56:41-08:00","id":1501816,"title":"","content":"A good amount of the ignorance around the Imbued is purely mundane: Lucifer is one of the least powerful characters aware of the potential to create Imbued sitting around unused. It's not that mages can't understand the Imbued, but to mages, the Imbued are a random emergent new thing that came out of nowhere, and the Imbued have some levels of protections from mages just magically digging into things about them. But an Innocent and a friendly mage can sit down and chat about what the Imbued are just fine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}